---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseStudySection from "../../components/CaseStudySection.astro";

const threads = [
  {
    key: "discover",
    label: "Find an event",
    owned: "Built search, filters, and maps around place, time, and taste.",
    enables: "A broad idea becomes a smaller set of events to choose from."
  },
  {
    key: "plan",
    label: "Make a plan",
    owned: "Built saved events and routes with ordering and arrival times.",
    enables: "People can organise several stops rather than keep a collection of open tabs."
  },
  {
    key: "return",
    label: "Share and return",
    owned: "Connected stable event links, saved state, and offline support.",
    enables: "A plan has a way back after the first visit, including when a connection is weak."
  }
];
const mechanisms = [
  {
    thread: "discover",
    layer: "Keep the map optional",
    detail: "Search and filters can do useful work before the MapLibre view loads. Geography adds context without making every visitor wait for a map."
  },
  {
    thread: "plan",
    layer: "Save a route as its own record",
    detail: "Postgres-backed plans retain stop order and arrival times. Saving a set of favourites alone would lose the sequence that makes it a night out."
  },
  {
    thread: "return",
    layer: "Keep identity separate from presentation",
    detail: "Canonical event keys let shared links refer to an event even when its listing changes. Browser snapshots and queued changes support returning to saved work during a poor connection."
  }
];
const initialThread = "discover";
---

<CaseStudyLayout title="Fête Finder Discovery" description="Search, maps, and saved routes that help people turn the Fête de la Musique programme into a night out." threads={threads} initialThread={initialThread}>
  <p slot="intro">I built search, maps, and saved routes to help people turn a city-wide programme into a night out. The June 2026 recap records 54,295 page views across the programme.</p>
  <dl slot="meta" class="case-meta" aria-label="Case study summary">
    <div><dt>Context</dt><dd>Out Of Office Collective / 2025–26</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Search, maps, route planning, sharing, offline support</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Project</dt><dd><a href="https://fete.outofofficecollective.co.uk">fete.outofofficecollective.co.uk</a></dd></div>
  </dl>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-problem" title="Problem">
    <p>People rarely start with an exact event title. They know an area, a genre, a time, or that they want something free nearby. Once they find a few options, they need to turn them into a route and share it with friends.</p>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-contribution" title="My contribution">
    <table class="case-ledger">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">What I built and why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{threads.map((thread) => (
        <tr data-thread={thread.key} data-active={thread.key === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
          <th scope="row">{thread.label}</th><td><p>{thread.owned}</p><p>{thread.enables}</p></td>
        </tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-decisions" title="Decisions">
    <div class="case-prose">
      <table class="case-ledger">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Choice</th><th scope="col">Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{mechanisms.map((mechanism) => (
          <tr data-thread={mechanism.thread} data-active={mechanism.thread === initialThread ? true : undefined}>
            <th scope="row">{mechanism.layer}</th><td>{mechanism.detail}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
      <figure class="case-diagram"><figcaption>From a vague idea to a shared plan</figcaption><ol>
<li><strong>Find</strong><span>Narrow the programme by place, time, and taste.</span></li>
<li><strong>Plan</strong><span>Save stops and decide when to arrive.</span></li>
<li><strong>Return</strong><span>Share the route and open it again later.</span></li>
</ol></figure>
    </div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-result" title="Recorded activity" summary="June 2026, from the archived production snapshot.">
    <div class="case-prose"><p>The product connects discovering an event, planning several stops, and sharing the result. The June 2026 recap records 54,295 page views and 10,270 outbound clicks, from the production backup taken on 3 July. These count page views and clicks, not unique people.</p></div>
  </CaseStudySection>

  <CaseStudySection id="case-lesson" title="Lesson">
    <p>Finding a good option is only the first part of discovery. The route home to a saved plan matters too: what happens when someone opens the link later, an organiser edits the details, or mobile reception drops?</p>
  </CaseStudySection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
